$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Decene Oxidation with Pd[(-)-sparteine]Cl2 and TBHP(aq) in DMA or NMP as
Solvent In a flame dried 5 mL round bottom flask equipped with a sidearm
and stir bar, 2.1 mg Pd[(-)-sparteine]Cl2 (0.005 mmol, 0.02 equiv.) and
175 μL TBHP(aq) (70 wt%, 1.25 mmol, 5.0 equiv.) were combined. The flask
was attached to a condenser on a 4-neck cow. The reaction mixture was
heated in an oil bath to 70 ˚C. After 5 minutes of vigorous stirring, 1
mL NMP or DMA was added. The solution stirred 10 minutes then 50 μL of
decene containing tetradecane internal standard was added (0.25 mmol, 1
equiv.). Aliquots (ca. 0.03 mL) of each reaction were periodically taken
via syringe and were analyzed using GC. Conversions were measured
relative to tetradecane internal standard.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM optimization study, optimized on oxidant, addnl. catalyst and DMA:water
ratio
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Discovery of a Practical Direct O2-Coupled Wacker Oxidation with
Pd[(-)-sparteine]Cl2
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Cornell, Candace N.; Sigman, Matthew S.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2006), 8(18), 4117-4120

