$DATUM 7732-18-5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedure for Palladium-Catalyzed Wacker Oxidant Using Oxygen as
the Oxidant A seal tube containing terminal olefins 1 (1 mmol) and
Pd(OAc)2 (10 mol %), was evacuated and filled with dioxygen gas using an
oxygen containing balloon. Then, DMSO (2.5 mL), H2O (0.25 mL) and
trifluoroacetic acid (TFA) (1 mmol) were sequentially added to the system
via syringe under an oxygen atmosphere. The reaction mixture was stirred
at 70 °C until completion of the reaction (TLC). Then the reaction was
cooled to RT and partitioned between water and ethyl acetate. The layers
were separated and the organic layer was washed with aqueous saturated
brine solution, dried over MgSO4, filtered and concentrated under reduced
pressure. Purification by flash chromatography. Methyl ketones 2.
1-Phenylethanone (2a)4 as light yellow oil; Yield 86% (eluent: ethyl
acetate/hexane = 1/100). 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ (ppm) 7.94 (d, J =
8.0 Hz, 2H), 7.55-7.52 (m , 1H), 7.43 (t, J = 8 Hz, 2H), 2.57 (s, 3H);
13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ (ppm) 26.6, 128.3, 128.5, 133.1, 137.0,
198.1.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, Tsuji-Wacker oxidation, Markonikov selectivity, optimized
on catalysts, reaction conditions, sealed tube used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Wacker-Type Oxidation and Dehydrogenation of Terminal Olefins Using
Molecular Oxygen as the Sole Oxidant without Adding Ligand
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Wang, Yu-Fei; Gao, Ya-Ru; Mao, Shuai; Zhang, Yan-Lei; Guo, Dong-Dong;
Yan, Zhao-Lei; Guo, Shi-Huan; Wang, Yong-Qiang
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2014), 16(6), 1610-1613

