$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 2.6. Catalytic Experiments. The Wacker
oxidation of unsaturated compounds was carried out in steel autoclaves at
an oxygen pressure of 0.5 MPa for 2 and 8 h within the temperature range
30-90 °C under intensive stirring in water or ionic liquid using the
corresponding supramolecular ligand and components of a catalytic system
with cocatalysts CuCl2 and CuCl2/ heteropolyacid (HPA). The products were
extracted with diethyl ether, and the organic layer was analyzed by
gas-liquid chromatography using hexadecane as an internal standard. The
analysis was conducted on a Chrompack CP9001 chromatograph with an SE-30
column (0.3 mm x 30 m). Yield 83%
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Pd salt assumed, Wacker oxidation
