$DATUM 7732-18-5
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Oxidation of 4-methylstyrene with Pd[(-)-sparteine]Cl2 and TBHP in MeOH
To a flame dried 5 mL round bottom flask equipped with a sidearm and stir
bar, 1.9 mg Pd[(-)-sparteine]Cl2 (0.0045 mmol, 0.015 equiv.) and 725 μL
MeOH were added. The flask was then attached to a condenser on a 4-neck
cow and placed under N2. The reaction mixture was heated in an oil bath
at 35 °C. After stirring for 10 minutes, 230 μL TBHP(aq) (70 wt%, 1.65
mmol, 5.5 equiv.) was added. The solution was stirred for 15 minutes then
40 μL of substrate containing 4-heptanone internal standard was added
(0.3 mmol, 1 equiv.). Aliquots (ca. 0.03 mL) of each reaction were
periodically taken via syringe and were analyzed using GC. Conversions
were measured relative to 4-heptanone internal standard. At 18.5h >99 %
conversion and 92 % GC yield of 4'-methylacetophenone was measured.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Discovery of a Practical Direct O2-Coupled Wacker Oxidation with
Pd[(-)-sparteine]Cl2
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Cornell, Candace N.; Sigman, Matthew S.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2006), 8(18), 4117-4120

