$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Styrene Hammett Analysis: To small vials were
weighed AgSbF6 (1.3 mg, 0.0038 mmol). A stirbar was added along with a
standard solution of Pd(Quinox)Cl2 (0.56 mg, 0.0015 mmol) in CH2Cl2. Next
70 wt% TBHP(aq) (644 μL, 4.5 mmol) was added followed by CH2Cl2 (1 mL) to
bring up to appropriate volume. The reaction mixtures were cooled along
with a standard solution of substrate in CH2Cl2. An appropriate amount of
the cooled substrate solution (0.15 mmol) was charged to the vials. After
addition of the substrate solution, aliquots (∼100 μL) were removed
periodically and passed through a silica pipet eluting with ethyl
acetate. These samples were then analyzed by gas chromatography and the
amount of product was measured relative to an internal standard of
dodecane (∼10 wt% as compared to substrate). All substrates were run in
duplicate and peak integrations were corrected with a response factor
from samples of known molar ratio. ligand: 3, X (mol % cat.): 5.0, time:
16h, conversion>99%, TON: 19. 97%product.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM in-situ generated catalyst, see experimental details, optimization study,
optimized on catalyst, alternative preparations shown, alternatively
reaction carried out by decreasing stoichiometry of catalyst decreased
yield, kinetics studied, selective oxidation, Wacker oxidation
