$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for Palladium-Catalyzed
Wacker Oxidant Using Oxygen as the Oxidant A seal tube containing
terminal olefins 1 (1 mmol) and Pd(OAc)2 (10 mol %), was evacuated and
filled with dioxygen gas using an oxygen containing balloon. Then, DMSO
(2.5 mL), H2O (0.25 mL) and trifluoroacetic acid (TFA) (1 mmol) were
sequentially added to the system via syringe under an oxygen atmosphere.
The reaction mixture was stirred at 70 °C until completion of the
reaction (TLC). Then the reaction was cooled to RT and partitioned
between water and ethyl acetate. The layers were separated and the
organic layer was washed with aqueous saturated brine solution, dried
over MgSO4, filtered and concentrated under reduced pressure.
Purification by flash chromatography. Methyl ketones 2.
1-(3-ChloroPhenyl)ethanone (2f)6 as light yellow oil; Yield 85% (eluent:
ethyl acetate/hexane = 1/100). 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.86 (d, J = 8.0
Hz, 1H), 7.77 (t, J = 8.0 Hz, 1H), 7.47 (t, J = 8.0 Hz, 1H), 7.36 (t, J =
8.0 Hz, 1H), 2.55 (s, 3H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ (ppm) 196.9,
138.8, 133.2, 130.1, 128.6, 126.6, 26.9.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, Tsuji-Wacker oxidation, Markonikov selectivity, sealed
tube used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Wacker-Type Oxidation and Dehydrogenation of Terminal Olefins Using
Molecular Oxygen as the Sole Oxidant without Adding Ligand
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Wang, Yu-Fei; Gao, Ya-Ru; Mao, Shuai; Zhang, Yan-Lei; Guo, Dong-Dong;
Yan, Zhao-Lei; Guo, Shi-Huan; Wang, Yong-Qiang
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2014), 16(6), 1610-1613

