$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for oxidation reactions with
PdCl2/CuCl for screening (method B) PdCl2 (0.1 eq) and CuCl (1.0 eq) were
placed in a Schlenk flask, and DMF and H2O (7:1, 0.05 M), and the
protected allylic amine (1.0 eq) were added. An oxygen filled balloon was
placed on top, and the mixture was stirred vigorously. The reaction was
monitored by GC-MS. After completion, CH2Cl2 (10 mL) and H2O (10 mL) were
added. The aqueous layer was extracted with CH2Cl2 (3 x 10 mL), the
combined organic layers washed with saturated aq. NaHCO3 solution and
H2O, and dried over MgSO4. The solvent was evaporated in vacuum.
3-(1,3-Dioxo-1,3-dihydro-isoindol-2-yl)-butyraldehyde (2h)
3-(1,3-Dioxo-1,3-dihydro-isoindol-2-yl)-4-phenyl-butyraldehyde (2m)
Column Chromatography (pentane:EtOAc =95:5) gave the aldehyde as
coulourless oil (94%). 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ=3.00 (dd, 2 J=18.0 Hz,
3 J=5.2 Hz, 1H; CH2), 3.13 (dd, 2 J=13.6 Hz, 3 J=6.8 Hz, 1H; CH2), 3.25
(dd, 2 J=13.4 Hz, 3 J=9.0 Hz, 1H; CH2), 3.39 (ddd, 2 J=18.1 Hz, 3 J=9.0
Hz, 4 J=1.5 Hz, 1H; CH2), 4.99-5.08 (m, 1H; CH), 7.11-7.25 (m, 5H; CH),
7.63-7.71 (m, 2H; CH), 7.72-7.78 (m, 2H; CH), 9.71 (s, 1H; CHO). 13C NMR
(100 MHz, CDCl3): δ=38.5 (CH2), 45.5 (CH2), 47.0 (CH), 123.2 (CH), 126.9
(CH), 128.6 (CH), 129.0 (CH), 131.5 (C), 133.9 (CH), 137.0 (C), 168.0
(CO), 199.1 (CHO). HR-ESI-MS: m/z calcd for C18H16NO3 [M+H]+ 294.1130,
found 294.1125.
