$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 6-Procedure for the synthesis of diketones
(Wacker oxidation) A mixture of olefin (1.0 equiv.), PdCl2 (10 mol%) and
Cu(OAc)2 (20 mol%) was dissolved in dimethyl acetamide: water (7:1, 0,1
M) solution. The reaction flask was purged with O2 and the reaction
mixture was stirred under O2 (1 atm.) for 24-48 hours (monitored by TLC).
The mixture was diluted in diethyl ether and washed with water (3 fold)
and brine. The organic was dried over magnesium sulfate, filtered and
concentrated. Diketone 36: The residue was purified by flash column
chromatography (silica gel, 1.5 cm diameter × 10.0 cm height; 1:9 ethyl
acetate: hexane) to yield diketone 36 (19.7 mg, 93%) as a colorless oil.
Rf = 0.16 (2:8, diethyl ether: hexane); [α]D2O -62.5° (c 0.99, CDCl3,
optical rotation was measured from a sample with 74% ee); 1H NMR (300
MHz, CDCl3) δ 8.23 (br s, 1H), 8.18 (d, J = 7.7 Hz, 1H), 7.80 (d, J = 7.8
Hz, 1H), 7.61 (t, J = 7.8 Hz, 1H), 3.80 (ddd, J = 10.7, 5.1, 3.0 Hz, 1H),
3.23 (dd, J = 18.2, 10.7 Hz, 1H), 2.62 (dd, J = 18.2, 3.0 Hz, 1H), 2.18
(s, 3H), 2.00 (dtd, J = 13.6, 6.7, 5.2 Hz, 1H), 0.96 (d, J = 6.8 Hz, 3H),
0.83 (d, J = 6.8 Hz, 3H); 13C NMR (126 MHz, CDCl3) δ 207.57, 201.99,
138.13, 131.76 - 130.63 (m, 2C), 129.31 - 129.05 (m, 2C), 125.21 (q, J =
3.8 Hz), 123.78 (q, J = 272.5 Hz), 47.16, 41.74, 29.95, 29.77, 21.35,
18.79; IR (neat) 3017, 3002, 2971, 2964, 2958, 2951, 2942, 2935, 2918,
2910, 2898, 2879, 2871, 2859, 1716, 1686, 1611, 1465, 1436, 1392, 1373,
1360, 1330, 1314, 1289, 1248, 1227, 1191, 1166, 1129, 1096, 1072, 986,
911, 803, 736, 696 cm-1; HRMS (ESI) calcd for C15H17F3O2 [M+H]+ 287.12534
and [M+Na]+ 309.10729, found [M+H]+ 287.12516 and [M+Na]+ 309.10799. ee
were determined by chiral HPLC. Separation condition: 5% i-PrOH/hexane,
Chiralcel OD-H, 1.0 mL/minute, RT: 6.02 min. and 7.19 min., ratio 15.31:
84.69. Molecular Weight: 286,29.
