$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure for oxidation reactions with
PdCl2/CuCl for screening (method B) PdCl2 (0.1 eq) and CuCl (1.0 eq) were
placed in a Schlenk flask, and DMF and H2O (7:1, 0.05 M), and the
protected allylic amine (1.0 eq) were added. An oxygen filled balloon was
placed on top, and the mixture was stirred vigorously. The reaction was
monitored by GC-MS. After completion, CH2Cl2 (10 mL) and H2O (10 mL) were
added. The aqueous layer was extracted with CH2Cl2 (3 x 10 mL), the
combined organic layers washed with saturated aq. NaHCO3 solution and
H2O, and dried over MgSO4. The solvent was evaporated in vacuum.
3-(1,3-Dioxo-1,3-dihydro-isoindol-2-yl)-butyraldehyde (2h)
3-(1,3-Dioxo-1,3-dihydro-isoindol-2-yl)-octanal (2i) Column
Chromatography (pentane:EtOAc = 2:1) gave the aldehyde as colourless oil
(91%). 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ=0.83 (t, 3 J=6.8 Hz, 3H; CH3), 1.20-
1.31 (m, 6H; CH2), 1.66-1.75 (m, 1H; CH2), 2.00-2.11 (m, 1H; CH3), 2.95
(dd, 2 J=18.0 Hz, 3 J=5.6 Hz, 4 J=1.1 Hz, 1H; CH2), 3.30 (dd, 2 J=17.6
Hz, 3 J=8.8 Hz, 1H; CH2), 4.76 (mc, 1H; CH), 7.70 (dd, 3 J=5.6 Hz, 4
J=3.2 Hz, 2H; CH), 7.82 (dd, 3 J=5.4 Hz, 4 J=3.0 Hz, 2H; CH), 9.74 (s,
1H; CHO). 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ=13.8 (CH3), 22.3 (CH2), 25.8 (CH2),
31.1 (CH2), 32.3 (CH2), 45.7 (CH2), 46.3 (CH), 123.2 (CH), 131.6 (C),
133.9 (CH), 168.2 (CO), 199.4 (CHO). HR-ESI-MS: m/z calcd for C16H20NO3
[M+H]+ 274.1438, found 274.1438.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM selective for the aldehyde, Wacker oxidation
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
