$DATUM 5R)-5-(2,4-Di-O-benzoyl-3,6-dideoxy-α -L-arabino-hexopyranosyl)
hexan-2-one (14) Pd(OAc)2 (8 mg, 36 mmol) and CuCl (4 mg, 40 mmol) were
added to a soln of 15 (90 mg, 205 mmol) in DMF (7 mL) and H2O (1 mL). The
mixture was stirred in an open flask at r.t. for 18 h. After addition of
sat. NH4Cl soln (20 mL) and Et2O (20 mL) the layers were separated. The
aqueous layer was extracted with Et2O (2 × 20 mL) and the combined
organic layers were dried (MgSO4). The solvent was removed and the
residue was purified by flash chromatography (silica gel, PE-Et2O, 3:1 to
2:1) to provide 14. Light yellow oil, yield 83 mg, 89%. IR (ATR): 2975,
2929, 1714, 1686, 1652, 1635, 1602, 1451, 1316, 1263, 1216, 1176, 1153,
1100, 1066, 1021, 942, 893, 853, 808, 709, 686 cm-1. 1H NMR (500 MHz,
CDCl3): δ = 1.20 (d, J = 6.1 Hz, 3 H), 1.28 (d, J = 6.3 Hz, 3 H),
1.84-1.89 (m, 2 H), 2.14-2.20 (m, 1 H), 2.20 (s, 3 H), 2.41 (dt, J =
13.5, 3.7 Hz, 1 H), 2.60 (t, J = 7.5 Hz, 2 H), 3.88 (sext, J = 6.1 Hz, 1
H), 4.05 (dq, J = 3.6, 6.3 Hz, 1 H), 4.93 (s, 1 H), 5.12 (m, 1 H), 5.17
(ddd, J = 14.5, 9.9, 4.6 Hz, 1 H), 7.44-7.48 (m, 4 H), 7.56-7.59 (m, 2
H), 8.03-8.05 (m, 2 H), 8.09-8.11 (m, 2 H). 13C NMR (DEPT, 125 MHz,
CDCl3): δ = 17.85 (CH3), 18.86 (CH3), 29.66 (CH2), 29.95 (CH3), 30.82
(CH2), 39.65 (CH2), 67.11 (CH),70.53 (CH), 71.06 (CH), 71.44 (CH), 93.55
(CH), 128.44 (4 CH), 129.61 (2 CH), 129.75 (C), 129.85 (2 CH), 129.92
(C), 133.21 (CH), 133.28 (CH), 165.64 (C=O), 165.78 (C=O), 208.42 (C=O).
MS (ESI): m/z = 339.1 [(M - C6H11O2)+], 472.1 [(M + NH4)+], 477.2 [(M +
Na)+].
