$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Synthesis of
3-[(1S*,3S*)-3-acetyl-3-(2-oxopropyl)cyclopentyl]-3-methylbutan-2-one
(6). To a stirred solution of palladium (II) chloride (300 mg, 1.69 mmol)
and copper (II) acetate monohydrate (3.38 g, 16.9 mmol) in
N,N-diemthylacetamide (5 mL) and H2O (0.8 mL) was added dropwise a
solution of 7 in N,N-dimethylacetamide (1 mL) at room temperature under
O2. After the reaction mixture was stirred for 3 days at room
temperature, the mixture was filtered under vacuo, and filtrate was
extracted with Et2O. The combined organic layers were washed with brine,
dried over MgSO4 . After the solvent was removed in vacuo, the resulted
residue was purified by column chromatography (hexane/AcOEt, 4:1. Yield:
(982 mg, 3.89 mmol, 86%) as yellow oil. IR (neat) 2972, 1715, 1695, 1682,
1471, 1361, 1170 cm-1; 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 1.04 (3H, s), 1.06 (3H,
s), 1.07-1.13 (1H, m), 1.25-1.43 (1H, m), 1.50 (1H, ddd, J = 3.6, 7.9,
13.0 Hz), 1.58-1.68 (1H, m), 1.96 (1H, ddd, J = 7.3, 9.2, 13.0 Hz),
2.08-2.16 (1H, m), 2.09 (3H, s), 2.10 (3H, s), 2.15 (3H, s), 2.20-2.36
(1H, m), 2.80 (1H, ½ABq, J = 18.0 Hz), 2.94 (1H, ½ABq, J = 18.0 Hz); 13C
NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3) δ 21.4, 21.7, 25.4, 25.5, 26.5, 30.2, 35.0, 36.7,
46.5, 49.0, 53.3, 55.7, 206.8, 210.9, 213.3; HRESIMS calcd for C15H25O3
[M+H]+ 253.1807, found 253.1804.
