$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM (S)-6-Azidononan-2-one (4). PdCl2 (210 mg, 1.18 mmol, 0.2 equiv) was
added to the N-methylpyrrolidone/water (30 mL/3.5 mL) solvent mixture,
and the suspension was stirred under O2 atmosphere (balloon) until PdCl2
had dissolved completely (approximately 1 h). Azide 12 (1.00 g, 5.99
mmol) was added, and the reaction mixture was stirred for 24 h at rt
under O2 atmosphere while maintaining a slight gas pressure
(approximately 1.25 bar). Water (30 mL) and Et2O(30 mL) were added, and
the mixture was stirred for 10 min. The aqueous layer was extracted with
Et2O (2 x 20 mL), combined organic phases were dried (Na2SO4), and the
solvent was evaporated in vacuo. The residue was purified by FLC (silica
gel, Et2O) to give azidoketone 4 (0.930 g, 85%). Compound 4: pale yellow
oil. (S)-6-Azidononan-2-one (4), yield (0.930 g, 85%). [α]20D +3.19 (c
1.66, CH2Cl2); IR (ATR) νmax 2958, 2933, 2873, 2094, 1715, 1457, 1410,
1359, 1271, 1250, 1162, 745 cm-1; 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 3.34-3.16
(1H, m, H-6), 2.47 (2H, t, H-3), 2.15 (3H, s, H-1), 1.60-1.76 (2H, m,
H-4), 1.37-1.56 (6H, m, H-5, H-7, H-8), 0.94 (3H, t, H-9); 13C NMR (75
MHz, CDCl3) δ 208.4 (C, C-2), 62.6 (CH, C-6), 43.2 (CH2, C-3), 36.4, 33.7
(2 x CH2, C-5, C-7), 29.9 (CH3, C-1), 20.3 (CH2, C-4), 19.3 (CH2, C-8),
13.9 (CH3, C-9); HRMS m/z 183.1453 (calcd for C9H17N3O, 183.1372).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, key intermediate, optimization study, optimized on
catalyst, optimized on solvent, optimized on reagent, optimized on
temperature, optimized on time, Wacker-Tsuji oxidation
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Efficient Total Synthesis of (+)-Dihydropinidine, (-)-Epidihydropinidine,
and (-)-Pinidinone
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
