$DATUM The one pot Claisen rearrangement3 using ethyl vinyl ether and mercuric
acetate transformed the allyl alcohols 3 into the enals 4. Oxidation of
the enals 4 using Wacker conditions4 generated the ketoaldehydes 5.
3-methyl-3-(4-methylphenyl)-4-oxo-pentanal 5a yield 85%. IR (neat): νmax
= 2740 (H-C=0), 1720 & 1705 (C=O), 1512, 1350 cm1. 'H NMR (90 MHz,
CDCl3): δ 9.62 (1 H, t, J=2.3 Hz, H-C=O), 7.19 (4 H, s, aromatic), 2.97
and 2.72 (2 H, d of AB q, J=17.1 and 2.3 Hz, H-2), 2.35 (3 H, s, Ar-CH3),
1.97 (3 H, s, CH3C=O), 1.69 (3 H, s, tert-CH3). 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3):
δ 209.1 (C=O), 201.3 (H-C=O), 137.9, 137.4, 129.8 (2 C) and 126.0 (2 C)
(aromatic), 53.8 (quaternary C), 52.1 (CH2CHO), 25.1 (CH3-C=O), 21.2 and
20.9 (2 x CH3).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM key step
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
