$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: The 4-pentenals 3a-h, PdCl2 (10 mol%), and
CuCl2 (10 mol%) were dissolved in aqueous DME (1:9) and stirred under an
oxygen atmosphere for 2-3 h. When the reaction was observed to be
complete, normal aqueous extractive work-up gave the ketoaldehydes 4a-h
in 71-84% yield. Compound 4b. liquid, yield 84% Bp/Mp [°C] (Torr): 123
(2.5); IR [cm-1] (neat/nujol): 2681.0, 1722.0, 1707.0; 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ J
(Hz): 1.62 (s, 3 H, -C-CH3), 2.11 (s, 3 H, -COCH3), 2.39 (s, 3 H, Ar-
CH3), 3.16 (s, 2 H, -CH2-CO), 7.42 (s, 4 H, Ar-H), 9.88 (s, 1 H, -CHO);
13C NMR (CDCl3) δ : 21.0 (Ar-CH3), 21.7 (-C-CH3), 27.8 (CH3-C=O), 49.1
(-CH2- C=O), 53.5 (Ar-C-CHO), 125.6 (Caromortho), 125.9 (Carommeta),
133.5 (Carom1), 135.4 (Carompara), 201.1 (-CHO), 206.6 (CH3-C=O);
Microanalysis calcd/found: C: 76.44 76.31; H: 7.90 8.01.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Wacker oxidation
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM An expedient protocol for cyclopentenone annulation
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Kulkarni, Mukund G.; Davawala, Saryu I.; Doke, Aniruddha K.; Pendharkar,
Dhananjay S.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthesis (2004), (17), 2919-2926

