$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: The 4-pentenals 3a-h, PdCl2 (10 mol%), and
CuCl2 (10 mol%) were dissolved in aqueous DME (1:9) and stirred under an
oxygen atmosphere for 2-3 h. When the reaction was observed to be
complete, normal aqueous extractive work-up gave the ketoaldehydes 4a-h
in 71-84% yield. Compound 4c. liquid, yield 83% Bp/Mp [°C] (Torr): 136
(0.6); IR [cm-1] (neat/nujol): 2695.0, 1716.0, 1707.0.; 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ
J (Hz): 1.19 (s, 3 H, -C-CH3), 1.83 (m, 2 H, -C-CH2-), 2.12 (s, 3 H,
-COCH3), 2.45 (t, 2 H, J = 8.6 Hz, Ar-CH2-), 2.69 (d, 1 H, J = 17.8 Hz,
-CO-CH2-), 2.84 (d, 1 H, J = 17.8 Hz, -COCH2-), 3.82 (s, 3 H, -OCH3),
3.84 (s, 3 H, -OCH3), 6.55-6.85 (m, 3 H, Ar-H), 9.58 (s, 1 H, -CHO); 13C
NMR (CDCl3) δ : 20.4 (C-CH3), 26.1 (CH3-C=O), 30.2 (Ar-CH2-), 34.4 (Ar-
CH2CH2), 46.2 (-CH2-C=O), 47.1 (-C-CHO), 55.8, 55.9 (2 × -OCH3), 113.5
(Carom5meta), 114.3 (Carom2ortho), 120.8 (Carom6ortho), 133.8 (Carom1),
145.4 (Carom4para), 147.8 (Carom3meta), 204.5 (-CHO), 206.4 (CH3-C=O);
Microanalysis calcd/found: C: 69.04 69.15; H: 7.97 7.99.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
