$DATUM The 4-pentenals 3a-h, PdCl2 (10 mol%), and CuCl2 (10 mol%) were dissolved
in aqueous DME (1:9) and stirred under an oxygen atmosphere for 2-3 h.
When the reaction was observed to be complete, normal aqueous extractive
work-up gave the ketoaldehydes 4a-h in 71-84% yield. Compound 4a. liquid,
yield 83% Bp/Mp [°C] (Torr): 121 (2.5); IR [cm-1] (neat/nujol): 2689.2,
1718.8, 1711.3.; 1H NMR (CDCl3) δ J (Hz): 1.56 (s, 3 H, -C-CH3), 2.04 (s,
3 H, -COCH3), 3.10 (s, 2 H, -COCH2-), 7.35 (s, 5 H, Ar-H), 9.66 (s, 1 H,
-CHO); 13C NMR (CDCl3) δ : 21.8 (-C-CH3), 27.9 (CH3- C=O), 48.9
(-CH2-C=O), 53.3 (Ar-C-CHO), 125.8 (Caromortho), 126.9 (Carompara), 128.6
(Carommeta), 137.1 (Carom1), 201.3 (-CHO), 206.7 (CH3-C=O); Microanalysis
calcd/found: C: 75.76 75.94; H: 7.42 7.38.
